From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 14:22:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09835/11362] [outer-loop] Third correction: a precondition DID
 fail; no model ever loaded

Corrects aaf899eca4, which corrected 613d227da1. Both prior texts are kept
verbatim in both files. This is the third pass over the same two entries by
the same author, and the sequence is left visible on purpose.

WHAT WAS WRONG THIS TIME. The first correction claimed no precondition
failed. One did. Both artifacts carry preconditions_checked as a 29-key dict
with all_required_preconditions_available=false and a populated
failed_preconditions: ['verification_commands'] for exp6581, and
['idle_supported_gpu','verification_commands'] for exp6582. The verdict
blocked_precondition_failed_without_quality_claim was accurate throughout.

HOW, because the mechanism matters more than the fact. The artifact was read
through a principle-unwrap helper:

    g = lambda k: (d.get(k).get('value') if isinstance(d.get(k), dict)
                   else d.get(k))

preconditions_checked IS a dict, so g returned .get('value'), got None, and
the field read as absent. A reader that assumes every dict is a principle
wrapper destroys every dict-valued field it touches. This is the same class
as the 2026-07-03 origin bug in the QA-Layer Authenticity Discipline, and an
agent refuted a claim of mine about that exact unwrap pattern earlier today
before I went and committed it myself.

THE ACTUAL CAUSE, from an independent diagnosis verified against the
artifacts: verification_commands at
experiment_6581_qwen36_flagship_source_shard.py:1513 requires the ENTIRE
project test suite to exit 0 before a model may load. No model was loaded in
either run. About 99.8% of each run was pytest, so 927s and 2411s are test
suite time, not GPU inference. The original reason text and the first
correction both describe live GPU work that never happened.

The check is wrongly placed and wrongly formed -- a precondition rather than
a post-work focused test, and a bare pytest that inherits coverage addopts --
but the suite is genuinely red repo-wide, 68 to 470 failures over twelve
days, so it reports a true fact. Demote and repair it; escalate the red suite
separately. Deleting it would hide a real problem.

exp6582's second failed precondition is probably self-inflicted:
idle_supported_gpu failed on a contended box, and this outer loop's own seed
sweep has held GPU 1 for over 19 hours.

RETIREMENT STATUS UNCHANGED. exp6582 stays retired on same-verdict-twice.
exp6581 stays un-retired on ran-once. Neither rests on the mechanism claims
corrected here, which is the only reason three passes of wrong reasoning did
not produce a wrong retirement. Verified: is_excluded 6581 False, 6582 True.

